Fix crash / queue evictions with movable CWSR pages on gfx1151 (Strix Halo)

Adapted for 10.2: the loader_context and registered-memory NonPaged
hunks are now upstream, and the libhsakmt fallback allocation is
non-paged unconditionally; only the SVM skip gate for the
StallOnRetryFault-era condition and the kernarg/coarse residency
hunk remain.
diff -ruN a/libhsakmt/src/queues.c b/libhsakmt/src/queues.c
--- a/libhsakmt/src/queues.c	2026-11-20 14:21:56.871692389 -0800
+++ b/libhsakmt/src/queues.c	2026-11-20 14:22:24.306755262 -0800
@@ -638,7 +638,16 @@
 		/* Allocate unified memory for context save restore
 		 * area on dGPU.
 		 */
-		if (!q->use_ats && ctx->hsakmt_is_svm_api_supported && svm_save_area) {
+		/* Strix Halo shares system DRAM with the CPU. Movable SVM CWSR
+		 * pages can evict all process queues during host compaction, even
+		 * when the application has pinned its own GPU-visible buffers.
+		 * Use the existing non-paged GTT path for these small queue areas;
+		 * retain SVM support for application-managed allocations.
+		 */
+		bool fixed_cwsr = node.EngineId.ui32.Major == 11 &&
+			node.EngineId.ui32.Minor == 5 && node.EngineId.ui32.Stepping == 1;
+		if (!q->use_ats && ctx->hsakmt_is_svm_api_supported && svm_save_area &&
+		    !fixed_cwsr) {
 			uint32_t size = PAGE_ALIGN_UP(q->total_mem_alloc_size);
 
 			pr_info("Allocating GTT for CWSR\n");
diff -ruN a/runtime/hsa-runtime/core/runtime/amd_memory_region.cpp b/runtime/hsa-runtime/core/runtime/amd_memory_region.cpp
--- a/runtime/hsa-runtime/core/runtime/amd_memory_region.cpp	2026-11-20 14:21:56.873722308 -0800
+++ b/runtime/hsa-runtime/core/runtime/amd_memory_region.cpp	2026-11-20 14:22:24.306828029 -0800
@@ -107,6 +107,12 @@
     mem_flag_.ui32.HostAccess = 1;
     mem_flag_.ui32.CachePolicy = HSA_CACHING_CACHED;
 
+    // HIP can obtain its kernel-argument and copy arenas from the coarse
+    // pool, bypassing ROCr's dedicated kernarg pool. Keep these runtime
+    // buffers resident too. Ordinary fine-grained allocations retain their
+    // existing policy; disabling USERPTR globally changes their performance.
+    if (kernarg || !fine_grain) mem_flag_.ui32.NonPaged = 1;
+
     if (kernarg) mem_flag_.ui32.Uncached = 1;
 
     virtual_size_ =
